# ---- Rust ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The build directory is the big one: several gigabytes of intermediates for a
# 13 MB binary.
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
*.profraw

# Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored. This is a binary crate, not a
# library: the lock file is what makes a build reproducible, and it is what CI
# builds from.

# ---- Flatpak -------------------------------------------------------------
# flatpak-builder writes all of these beside the manifest. The build trees
# inside .flatpak-builder hold the extracted sources for x264, x265 and ffmpeg,
# and reach several gigabytes on their own.
.flatpak-builder/
build-dir/
repo/
*.flatpak
*.flatpakref

# packaging/flatpak/cargo-sources.json is NOT ignored. It is generated, but a
# Flathub submission has to carry it -- which is the whole point of generating
# it.

# ---- What the platform packaging scripts produce -------------------------
# build.ps1 and bundle.sh both write into dist/; the rest is what they leave
# behind when run from somewhere else.
dist/
*.zip
*.dmg
*.msi
*.exe
*.app/

# ---- Editors and IDEs ----------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
.zed/
.helix/
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
*.swp
*.swo
*~
\#*\#
.\#*

# ---- Operating system leavings -------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---- Profiling, coverage, crash dumps ------------------------------------
perf.data
perf.data.old
flamegraph.svg
/coverage/
*.gcda
*.gcno
core
core.[0-9]*

# ---- Local machine state -------------------------------------------------
# Per-checkout settings and environment, none of which belongs to anyone else.
.claude/settings.local.json
.direnv/
.envrc
*.log

# The test suite writes its settings to APRICOT_CONFIG_DIR and its fixtures to
# the system temporary directory, so neither lands here -- but a run pointed at
# the tree would put them in one of these.
/scratch/

# ---- Kept locally, not carried in the repo -------------------------------
# Windows and macOS are not shipped yet, and their packaging scripts are the
# only part of the tree that exists purely to serve them. They still work from
# a checkout of this machine -- they are simply not what the repository is for.
# The three packaging files beside them stay tracked: tests/units.rs compiles
# the manifest, the desktop entry and the metainfo in and asserts on them.
/packaging/windows/
/packaging/macos/

# The built bundle is a release asset, uploaded to the release page rather than
# committed. Already matched by *.flatpak above; named here so it is obvious.
/apricot-studio.flatpak

# ---- Generated, but still committed --------------------------------------
# assets/icon-256.png is rendered from the SVG, and src/main.rs pulls it in
# with include_bytes!, so a checkout without it does not compile. It stays
# tracked; this note exists so nobody adds it to the list above.
